  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Introduced Build 625  (and in  2018.3.1 Open Beta), visual error with arms not respecting the prone idle animation, as arms are always following the camera. Issue as the hands always following  the head conflicts with custom idle positions that animate the body and arms in poses like \"sleeping\" and thus prevent the use of them in desktop with this new control feature for proning.\n\nSuggest making the arms  follow the prone animation at times they are not used in desktop.  \n\nSteps to duplicate:   Observe how your arms follow your head when proning in desktop. Auxiliary test, use a custom prone where the hands look best resting with the body and observe the miss-match.\n\nUntested but It is plausible the arms to head rigging may conflict these sleepy animations in VR mode as well, IF deactivating the controllers (which makes arms follow the animation) now make the arms follow the head in VR.\n\nPhoto shows desktop arms following head in prone, in a world that allows the user to mirror view upwards. One arm should be behind the head and the other behind the back.",
